hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3042","Narrated to us Al-Rabee’ from Al-Shaafi’i, who reported from Ibn ‘Uyaynah, who said: I heard Al-Zuhri narrating from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Ibn ‘Abbaas (RA) that a woman from Khath’am asked the Prophet (ﷺ) and he mentioned the hadith, and he said: Sufyaan said: “This is how I preserved it from Al-Zuhri.” And ‘Amr ibn Deenaar reported to me from Al-Zuhri from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Ibn ‘Abbaas (RA) a similar narration and he added: She said: “O Messenger of Allah, will this benefit him?” He said: “Yes, just as if he had a debt upon him and you paid it off, it would benefit him.”\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
